WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.020
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:05.300
Greetings from extremely muggy Florida. I have one day off this month, and you'll never guess where I spent it.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.520
Lego Land!

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:10.180
This place is great, but I wouldn't necessarily characterize it as relaxing.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:11.700
Hank, I'm on I-4 in Orlando,

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:17.020
and I'm remembering that, like, 12 years ago you had a viral hit website called ihatei-4.com,

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:18.620
and it just - it made me smile.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.520
Anyway, it's gonna take me a while to get to the next place,

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.660
but I'm gonna use movie magic to get you there quicker.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:25.960
And...we've arrived, just like that!
It took 45 minutes.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.400
I have five minutes until my Runners' World photo shoot.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.860
That's right! I'm doing a photo shoot for the magazine Runners' World.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:34.300
I am now literally a fitness model.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:38.300
I mean, so majestic! 
Is that a middle-aged person or a gazelle?

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.543
Okay Hank, I am now at your old high school, 
and I gotta go sign some books.

00:00:41.543 --> 00:00:42.780
Brief pause for book signing.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:46.980
Alright so first off, quick thank-you to the Winter Park High School students who made this paper town.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:52.300
They also got us t-shirts and special green green room chairs and a chair for our secret brother Dave.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:56.000
But most importantly, they got Hank's high school yearbook.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:58.000
Look at tiny baby Hank!

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.920
Look at Hank's high school yearbook photo. Oh my god!

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:04.580
"Brian Beck and Hank Green enjoy some quality time surfing the 'net.'

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:07.400
They believe that internet privileges should be given to all seniors!"

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.800
Hank, I agree!

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:12.420
Hello, and greetings from the future because the rest of my Orlando footage got corrupted.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:15.120
We are now in...Nashville?

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.900
So Hank, this has been an awesome week.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:19.100
We've performed in front of more than 10,000 people,

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:23.240
including our spouses and children and parents and elementary school teachers.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:26.600
Turtles All the Way Down has reached number one on Amazon's bestseller list.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.720
It's also gotten extremely generous reviews,

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:32.840
including maybe the two best reviews any of my books have ever received.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.480
I'll link to those in the doobly-doo below.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:40.320
And also reading people's incredibly thoughtful 
responses to the book has brought me to tears 
again and again this week.

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.320
But it's also been a really difficult week.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:45.820
Like my mental health, to speak frankly, is not where I would like it to be.

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:49.560
Partly because I am so far outside my usual routine.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:54.540
And while I do really love to tour and talk with people about the book, it's also a bit overwhelming.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:56.640
So Hank, I hope you'll forgive this moment of sincerity,

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:04.060
but watching you perform at your old high school last night, I kept thinking about how incredibly kind you've been to me the last few weeks.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:08.440
Like, you're taking a month away from your family and your many jobs to be on tour with me,

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:12.180
you turned your freaking Twitter profile into actual Turtles All the Way Down,

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:18.080
and you've just been there for me so consistently in a way that frankly goes back to when you were a student at that high school.

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:22.240
I am really lucky and really grateful. Thank you.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:23.380
Yeah, that was way too much.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:27.440
You gotta cut the sentimentality somehow. 
You gotta say something mean about him now.

00:02:27.445 --> 00:02:29.040
I'm not very good at cutting insults.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.760
But I know someone who is.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.980
Hey Alice, say something silly about Uncle Hank.

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:35.340
[Laughter]

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.480
That works, thanks. I love you.  Bye.

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.200
Hank, you have a stupid butt.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:44.400
That is a direct quote from my four-year-old daughter.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:47.530
It's also kind of true with the ulcerative colitis and everything.

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:48.740
I'll see you on Friday.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:52.240
Actually, I'll see you like, five minutes from now.

